#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Independent audit of an Opacra chain: checks every block against the coin's rules.

Run on a machine with a synced node (normally a seed):
  opacra-audit                         testnet node on 127.0.0.1:29971, whole chain
  opacra-audit --rpc 127.0.0.1:29961   mainnet node
  opacra-audit --to 20160              stop at a given height (default: 10 blocks below the tip)
  opacra-audit --report audit.txt      also write the report to a file

It recomputes from the published rules, not from the node's code: every block reward
(emission curve, launch slow start, tail emission), every development fund payment (5% of
the subsidy, paid to the fund's one-time key and found with the fund's public view key),
every block's difficulty (LWMA-1), the chain links and the timestamp rule, and the total
coins created. Only the Python standard library is used, including the Keccak and
ed25519 arithmetic. Exit status 0 = every check passed, 1 = a check failed, 2 = could not
run.
"""

